          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            One can view the concept of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphism"} morphism
            or arrow in a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
            as an extreme abstraction of the concept of a spatial trajectory. It therefore comes with no surprise that (notions of) paths stemming from various conceptualizations of ‘space’ like e.g.
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quivers"} quivers
            or
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+spaces"} topological spaces
            arrange themselves in appropriate categories thereby giving rise to several
            %em different notions
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %strong path category
          %h2#free_category_on_a_directed_graph Free category on a directed graph
          %p
            There is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/forgetful+functor"} forgetful functor
            from
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/small+category"} small
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/strict+category"} strict
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/categories"} categories
            to
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quivers"} quivers
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+adjoint"} left adjoint
            %strong
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+category"} free category
            or
            %strong path category
            of a quiver, whose
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/objects"} objects
            are the vertices of the quiver. The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphisms"} morphisms
            from
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi a
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a
            to
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi b
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b
            in this free category are
            %em not
            merely the arrows from
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi a
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a
            to
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi b
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b
            in the quiver but instead are
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/lists"} lists
            of the form
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi a
                    %mi n
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi f
                    %mi n
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi a
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo −
                      %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %mi …
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi a
                    %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi f
                    %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi a
                    %mn 0
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (a_n,f_n,a_{n-1},\ldots,a_{1},f_1,a_0)
            where
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                  %mo ≥
                  %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \geq 0
            is a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+number"} natural number
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi a
                    %mn 0
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi a
                    %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %mi …
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi a
                    %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a_0,a_1,\ldots,a_n
            are vertices of the graph,
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi a
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mi a
                      %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a = a_0
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi b
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mi a
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b = a_n
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 0
                    %mo &lt;
                    %mi i
                    %mo ≤
                    %mi n
